1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.735
We're working on the plan for

2
00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.770
the first feature in the project roadmap.

3
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.972
We finished the feature spec.

4
00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.475
Let's do the full implementation of this feature.

5
00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.478
Just to refresh ourselves,

6
00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.581
we do a quick review of this feature specs plan.

7
00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.417
This was the first feature, hello Hono.

8
00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.787
The feature spec documents have what we need.

9
00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.791
To start your implementation, you'll want to clear out your context

10
00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.893
with a /clear command.

11
00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.996
Let's go back to the agent and enter a prompt

12
00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.399
to implement all the task groups.

13
00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.702
Sometimes you might choose to do task groups one at a time

14
00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.872
for even smaller steps and commits.

15
00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.575
This technique is especially helpful for areas where small mistakes

16
00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.477
can compound later,

17
00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:47.580
like in security or database management.

18
00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.284
While Claude is running, you can observe the changes

19
00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:55.288
it displays in the console to see its progress in real time.

20
00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.391
Afterwards, we can watch for the final changes

21
00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.294
in the commit window and visit the changes.

22
00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.230
This gives us an early jump on reviewing the work.

23
00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.435
This is the key role of the developer in such a paradigm,

24
00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.638
to act as an architect or supervisor

25
00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:16.342
and ensure that the agent is provided with a clear contract.

26
00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.846
We can also see the summary of what was done.

27
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.783
As you can see, the agent provides extra details

28
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:27.187
on the work performed for each of the task groups.

29
00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.857
Now, let's go to the package.json file.

30
00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.494
And in there, let's run the app.

31
00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.397
The server starts in the console.

32
00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.770
The browser shows the result of this feature spec.

33
00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:47.040
Not much. We said nano,

34
00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.943
but it's a good feeling to see pixels on the screen.

35
00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.045
We just implemented a feature.

36
00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.247
The agent did its validation.

37
00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.616
In the next lesson, we'll do ours.
